    {
     "type": "Text",
     "title": "",
     "description": "",
     "url": "https://www.are.na/block/52021500",
     "text": "Motion Paint\nInteractive Art with Arduino\nMotion Paint is an interactive art project that lets users draw colorful, glowing designs using hand movements tracked by a webcam.\nBuilt with Arduino and Python, it features a flex sensor for swirling effects, a knob to control brush size, a button to switch modes, copper touch pads, and colorful LED lights that respond to interactions.\nThe project combines physical controls, motion tracking, and digital art to create a fun, hands-on drawing experience."
    }
