   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "Text",
     "title": "Description",
     "description": "",
     "url": "https://www.are.na/block/52021543",
     "text": "Gizmo\nThis is a physical axis-gizmo that sends out variable voltage to an RGB LED depending on how close the probe is to the center of the gizmo on different axes.\nEach of the three axes correspond to a different color input on the LED. The probe inputs voltage to the axis when they make contact, and the axis is made of carbon Velostat, making the axes act as variable resistors that change voltage depending on where the probe is located on each axis.\nA further iteration on this device could be used for inputting location in 3d space into a device, or measuring the dimensions of an object."
    },
